{"uid":"e85c6f81d4268cca","name":"test_resume_reprotects_the_record_before_plan_review_child_runs","fullName":"tests.test_tasks_record_docker#test_resume_reprotects_the_record_before_plan_review_child_runs","historyId":"75562e3495d7dbb107c2c40e5dfd85ba","time":{"start":1791961513888,"stop":1791961525265,"duration":11377},"description":"Requirement B.5's second hole, closed by `migrate_task_record`'s own\n    unconditional re-protect: `release_protected_tasks_dir` hands the\n    record mount back to the agent's own uid at shutdown, and neither of\n    the two prior existing-record tests here ever inspects the directory\n    before the resumed engine's own NEXT authoritative write has already\n    re-protected it as a side effect -- so a resumed container's\n    `plan_review` hat child, itself a fully dropped agent-uid child,\n    previously ran while the directory was still agent-writable, renamed\n    it aside and planted a substituted document, and both `RunDir.\n    read_tasks()` and the real `GET /tasks` API believed it. This test\n    holds the resumed container in `plan_review`, attacks the record from\n    inside it via the engine's own `privsep.agent_child_kwargs()` posture,\n    and requires the authoritative record to survive.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Requirement B.5's second hole, closed by <code>migrate_task_record</code>'s own<br />\nunconditional re-protect: <code>release_protected_tasks_dir</code> hands the<br />\nrecord mount back to the agent's own uid at shutdown, and neither of<br />\nthe two prior existing-record tests here ever inspects the directory<br />\nbefore the resumed engine's own NEXT authoritative write has already<br />\nre-protected it as a side effect -- so a resumed container's<br />\n<code>plan_review</code> hat child, itself a fully dropped agent-uid child,<br />\npreviously ran while the directory was still agent-writable, renamed<br />\nit aside and planted a substituted document, and both <code>RunDir. read_tasks()</code> and the real <code>GET /tasks</code> API believed it. This test<br />\nholds the resumed container in <code>plan_review</code>, attacks the record from<br />\ninside it via the engine's own <code>privsep.agent_child_kwargs()</code> posture,<br />\nand requires the authoritative record to survive.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791958529132,"stop":1791958529132,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791958529132,"stop":1791958529132,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"work_root","time":{"start":1791961271812,"stop":1791961271813,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"gateway_ip","time":{"start":1791961271813,"stop":1791961271828,"duration":15},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"test_image","time":{"start":1791961271829,"stop":1791961492332,"duration":220503},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791961513886,"stop":1791961513886,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"at